OOGFOSJSExposeHostConstructor bridges original JS_InitClass semantics:
- obtains the actual, protected GFOS JSHostClass prototype using
  Object.getPrototypeOf on a registered JS_Wrap host instance
- exports a named unconstructable global Ship constructor whose .prototype
  IS the same object (including for independent ship wrappers)
- preserves prototype.constructor and instanceof checks
- re-export of same constructor is idempotent; invalid JS names rejected
- no added or changed javascript.library vectors; no SpiderMonkey ABI claims

Executed the entire unmodified original oolite-global-prefix.js, not a
rewritten or shortened version. It installed its documented prototype
extensions, global properties and worldScriptNames. The native Ship.spawn
method returned a test fixture object with index 0=42, and the ORIGINAL
Ship.prototype.spawnOne() returned 42 on shipA; shipB remained untouched.
This demonstrates genuine host-prototype extension without adapting each
script-defined method individually.

IMPORTANT LIMIT: Only Ship was a real GFOS JSHostClass wrapper. The remaining
original script classes (Mission, SystemInfo, System, SoundSource, Script,
Vector3D) used explicitly declared JS test-fixture constructors; these
must be native classes for a full game startup. This is not a playable Oolite
release or a proof that all original OOJS class hooks are equivalent.
